{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1122064-how-does-forum-play-work-exactly","id":1122064,"title":"How does forum play work exactly?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-28T14:47:45-07:00","id":1122064,"title":"How does forum play work exactly?","content":"Hi folks,<br /> <br /> I consider myself a veteran GM, got 25 years of experience under my belt. Through dedication and endurance, I managed to keep my players together and belong to the lucky few who can still play regurlarly in my mid-30s. But honestly, I never understood play by forum games. I browsed through the websides, but I don\u00b4t get at all how it is organised? How do GMs work? What is exactly captured in a thread and who starts it? How can a GM do his job, since mostly I don\u00b4t find there decisions in the thread?<br /> <br /> Can someone enlighten me to this part of the hobby I missed?<br /> <br /> Thanks and keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:57:17-07:00","id":1122070,"title":"","content":"Slowly and with a lot more managing of players than at the table. Somehow. There's a reason I haven't played forum games in the last 3 years. It is draining for the GM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T15:03:38-07:00","id":1122072,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m browsing through the Edge of Darkness Forum but I can\u00b4t make out, where the GM acts. I don\u00b4t know how these threads open, when and where the GM organises. I am very curious how that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T19:43:16-07:00","id":1122877,"title":"","content":"I have run games in real time that are text based over Google hangouts/Roll20 And it's a lot like table top, but you just have to wait a little longer for responses. I planned and prepared everything like normal. <br /> <br /> However play by post I have only run a game when its dm and player.. just one. mostly just the same. you drop the clues when you can after you read their posts and react accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:56:52-07:00","id":1123020,"title":"","content":"There is 2 forms of PBP in forums.<br /> <br /> First one is the unithread. The one you would see here for example, in which the DM narrates in his post and the players each respond in the same thread. Easy to follow as its all contained on the same thread.<br /> <br /> Second one is the PBP forum. Which is a entire forum dedicated to a single game with various threads ala Edge of darkness. The way it function is that anyone can start a scene (thread) and follow it to their conclusion with the DM posting as the NPCs and the players responding with their character action and line of thoughts. However the timeline is incredibly iffy. As you could start a scene on say Monday which includes all the PCs which might drag on and last until Friday but on Wednesday you start another scene. Which technically happens after the scene started on Monday but as that scene is still in flux, it could mess up the continuity by say, your character dies in the Monday scene. Normally, people who DM PBP forums play loose and fast with continuity.<br /> <br /> The advantages of unithread is that it offers a level of detail bigger than face to face because reading a long descriptive scene that allow for re reads is a lot easy on the mind that if a DM start describing while talking for 5+ minutes. It also allows for better exploring the character mindsets and inner working on his mind and better description on their powers or even styles. That some players wouldn't otherwise do in face to face by fear of hogging the spotlight or talking to much.<br /> <br /> The disadvantage is of course combat and posting frequency as being all in a single thread the DM cant really split the party without difficulties as one can do in face to face because in the latter you get immediate response while in posting a PC could take weeks while the rest take days to respond and just stop the whole game.<br /> <br /> Combat is another issue because normally on Face to face the back and forth of information is quicker. Going by<br /> &quot;DM establish the situation&quot;<br /> &quot;player propose an action or ask a question&quot;<br /> &quot;DM approves of action or answers a question&quot;<br /> &quot;DM or player assemble their dice roll&quot;<br /> &quot;Players decides to go ahead with the roll&quot;<br /> &quot;DM interprets the roll&quot;<br /> <br /> This process that in face to face could take minutes at most, could strecht on days on PBP. By sending and receiving PMs. Some games uses skype or other apps to speed the back and forth but even then the process could stretch for hours.<br /> <br /> PBP forums on the hand have the advantage of allowing a player run what i call masturbatory scenes, in which his PC interacts with NPCs of the player creation and only affect him. They are a wonderful way to explore the character and know more about it or really get into his skin. Or the same kind of scene with 2 pcs that doesnt really advance the plot in any way or form but instead delves into the psychology of them.<br /> <br /> For example i played in a Apocalypse PBP game and we ran a scene in which my character and another just were chilling in a sofa and discussing the latest marvel movie. Or i would start a scene which describes my character preparing himself for a funeral and all the emotions that went over his mind doing so.<br /> <br /> The disadvantages is the previously mention issues with combat, the iffy timeline, how taxing is on the DM, mechanics that are designed for face to face but not PBP like willpower (how much willpower one should have? if the timeline is wonky) or power/effects that last for a &quot;day&quot;. The other issue comes from the players themselves and how open the game is to recruiting. If it isnt open then no problem the DM selects a group he like and get along just fine.<br /> <br /> However if the game is open to recruitment the issues of cliques, favoritism and egos starts rising. Is the nature of the medium, one really gets attached to their character. Dms have their &quot;favorite&quot; group of player (friends or players that really mesh with their style) or previous experience with players that tries to derail the whole game or &quot;win&quot; makes them wary of allowing things outside of their comfort zone to new players but allow them to their known ones or just adopt a draconian ruling in a feeble effort to assert authority. Some players (normally the cliques) start seeing all the other PCs as NPCs in their PCs story and feel threatened when another pc competes with them. The characterization goes out of the window when PCs accepts the actions that makes no sense for them to accept just because their players like each other.<br /> <br /> All of this is avoidable by either the game not being open recruitment so the groups is small enough that the issues of cliques isnt so pronounce or with a DM being on top of things and try for everyone to have fun.<br /> <br /> Just a quick clarification: I use Edge of darkness as an example of the model of PBP forums but i have not played in it but in others PBP forums. So i am not attacking or saying anything bad about Edge of Darkness forums but just mention the issues i have run into in others PBP forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-31-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:34:16-07:00","id":1123044,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13653\" data-vbnamecard=\"13653\">Narr666</a> Are you planning on trying to run a PBP in a forum or doing something in real time /text based?<br /> <br /> I can chat with you more and tell you what has worked for me and what hasn't. If you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:18:55-07:00","id":1126469,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the late answer, I was away. Don\u00b4t really plan anything, just curious for academic reason. But a chat would be okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date